    "discoverySemantics": "company-discovery correctly leaves PROBABLE, AMBIGUOUS, and other non-auto-attach identities as outcome possible with company null and report companyId null. This preserves the review boundary between safe canonical attachment and uncertain identity.",
    "trustedReuseBoundary": "Reuse inside discovery is domain-first and requires exact-domain VERIFIED/VERIFIED_EXISTING COMPANY_PROFILE_RESOLUTION provenance or confirmed firmographics. JYRA_DISCOVERY provenance alone is intentionally insufficient.",
    "conflation": "The runner conflated resolving a frozen known-target benchmark with discovering possible market companies and interpreted the intentional absence of an auto-attached companyId as invalid provisioning.",
    "notProviderFailure": "All 10 persisted COMPANY_DISCOVERY runs SUCCEEDED with one call each, 90 total results, no provider errors, and the correct reference entity at rank 1 for every control.",
    "notProfileResolutionRegression": "Rank-1 profile resolution was not attempted and persisted LinkedIn remained null, so this failure did not occur in profile resolution. Provider-free profile-resolution regressions A-L passed.",
    "notCompanyLikenessRegression": "No rank-1 candidate was NOT_A_COMPANY. Provider-free identity normalization (100 rows) and regressions A-J passed, including company-likeness and service-label protections.",
    "notDatabaseMismatch": "The approved development database, Aadit Technologies tenant, GTM-Q1 project, and approved Managed SOC pack were confirmed; every exact canonical record was linked to the target project.",
    "gitLabDataQuality": "GitLab also has an unlinked duplicate f685c762-98f6-41a3-a582-0e9d478909b0 at gitlab.com. This is secondary data quality and cannot explain the all-ten failure.",
    "reviewBoundary": "PROBABLE does not grant canonical auto-attachment. The divergence is that a benchmark with an already-linked canonical target was made dependent on a fresh discovery candidate auto-attachment."
  },
